# Prompt budget (token thrift)

These habits save usage. They do **not** change app code or the OS.

## Context
- Prefer Grep/Glob + small file slices over reading whole files.
- Do not pull `@codebase` / wide folders unless the user asked for a repo-wide search.
- Skip lockfiles, `vendor/`, `node_modules/`, SQL dumps, logs, PDFs, and `.env` unless explicitly required.
- Summarize tool/terminal output; never paste large logs into the reply.

## Edits & replies
- Smallest diff that ships the ask. No drive-by refactors or unrelated files.
- Concise answers (a few sentences per point). No essay unless the user asks.
- Do not create markdown docs the user did not request.
- Prefer Ask / targeted edits over multi-tool Agent loops when the task is a single known file.

## Chat hygiene (tell user if relevant)
- One feature/bug per chat; suggest a new chat when the topic changes.
